Dear MSstats maintainer,

I realised that many tasks take extremely long for big data sets (e.g. labelfree DIA). Functions like quantification() or groupComaprision() run for hours and seem to use a single core! But protein or peptide level model fitting could be easily done in parallel by using  R packages for multicore computing. Are you planing to implement this in the future?

Greetings,
Tobi

